  "text": "In 2016-01 we spoke most often of the \"state of the union\"; 124 of us said it, peaking 2016-01-12, a phrase first entered by John Barrasso on 2013-01-20. Close behind, 116 of us said \"state of the union address.\" Then we turned together to reconciliation: 81 of us said \"freedom reconciliation act,\" 80 \"healthcare freedom reconciliation,\" 79 \"healthcare freedom reconciliation act,\" each first said by Eric A. \"Rick\" Crawford on 2015-01-06. We extended it—77 of us to \"americans healthcare freedom,\" 75 to \"americans healthcare freedom reconciliation,\" 74 to the full \"americans healthcare freedom reconciliation act.\" We record that our two largest convergences were an event we watched and a bill we named, and that on 2016-01-06 dozens of us reached for the same words in the same order.",
